WEBVTT

00:00:00.564 --> 00:00:05.434
Yume kara samete mo
Even if I wake from my dreams

00:00:06.464 --> 00:00:11.934
Kono te wo nobasu yo
I'll reach my hand out to you

00:00:23.454 --> 00:00:28.724
Onaji tsuyosa de yobi au
If our hearts can reach each other

00:00:29.454 --> 00:00:34.084
Kokoro ni nareru no naraba
with the same strength

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:40.594
Nanninbun no kizu demo
Then I would be able to bare

00:00:41.134 --> 00:00:46.264
Boku wa uketome rareru yo
The pain of many hearts

00:00:46.674 --> 00:00:50.204
Mousukoshi datte kiga surun da
I can feel that it will arrive soon

00:00:50.284 --> 00:00:55.274
Kono kabe ga kuzureru
When these walls will be torn down

00:00:56.084 --> 00:01:00.424
Reimei
The dawn

00:01:02.154 --> 00:01:08.114
Yume kara samete mo
mada minai yume no houmade
Even if we wake from our dreams
We'll have to keep running

00:01:08.194 --> 00:01:14.104
Bokura wa hitori de
hashiri tsuzukeru shika nain da
Towards our unrevealed dreams

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:20.734
Korogari mayotte tsukuri dasu
boku no inryoku ga
The gravity by my painful journey
will draw me

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:26.954
Itsuka kimi e
To you one day

00:01:40.464 --> 00:01:43.024
Isn't that the guy from
the Twilight Brigade?

00:01:43.094 --> 00:01:46.334
He's the PC that the brigade
and TaN were fighting over.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:49.424
It's amazing they destroyed TaN.

00:01:49.774 --> 00:01:52.604
I can't believe TaN cheated.

00:01:53.104 --> 00:01:55.734
They fell into the Brigade's trap
and got exposed, right?

00:01:56.214 --> 00:01:57.044
Yeah.

00:02:04.184 --> 00:02:05.214
Haseo!

00:02:05.454 --> 00:02:07.484
Hey, isn't it amazing?

00:02:07.554 --> 00:02:10.524
Haven't you heard?
We're really famous now!

00:02:10.994 --> 00:02:12.084
You know what...

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:13.594
Shut up!

00:02:13.794 --> 00:02:19.564
Even if we have no words

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:21.664
Could we continue

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:25.674
Singing like the wind

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:26.814
In the same way

00:02:26.814 --> 00:02:27.214
In the same way
Uh...

00:02:27.214 --> 00:02:27.244
In the same way

00:02:27.244 --> 00:02:27.874
In the same way
Huh?

00:02:27.874 --> 00:02:28.274
In the same way

00:02:28.274 --> 00:02:29.644
In the same way
Uh, well, you know...

00:02:29.644 --> 00:02:29.674
Uh, well, you know...

00:02:29.674 --> 00:02:30.314
We are able to love people
Uh, well, you know...

00:02:30.314 --> 00:02:30.344
We are able to love people

00:02:30.344 --> 00:02:31.484
We are able to love people
Shino?

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:31.684
We are able to love people

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.684
We are able to love people
She hasn't logged in yet.

00:02:33.684 --> 00:02:34.054
We are able to love people

00:02:34.054 --> 00:02:35.954
We are able to love people
I bet she'll be surprised!

00:02:35.954 --> 00:02:35.984
We are able to love people

00:02:35.984 --> 00:02:36.954
We are able to love people
Because we're famous now!

00:02:36.954 --> 00:02:36.984
Because we're famous now!

00:02:36.984 --> 00:02:38.554
Without being taught?
Because we're famous now!

00:02:38.554 --> 00:02:48.484
Without being taught?

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:54.394
Speak of the devil.

00:02:54.904 --> 00:02:55.664
What?

00:02:57.874 --> 00:02:59.934
Has Ovan been in contact yet?

00:03:00.004 --> 00:03:01.034
Not yet.

00:03:02.174 --> 00:03:03.784
- Don't you think this is a bit weird!

00:03:03.784 --> 00:03:04.804
- Don't you think this is a bit weird!
- Don't yell!

00:03:05.444 --> 00:03:07.104
I wasn't talking to you.

00:03:07.484 --> 00:03:10.084
We fought for
the Key of the Twilight...

00:03:10.084 --> 00:03:11.624
Even if the universe shall end
We fought for
the Key of the Twilight...

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:11.654
Even if the universe shall end

00:03:11.654 --> 00:03:13.384
Even if the universe shall end
...and believed in Ovan.

00:03:13.384 --> 00:03:14.794
Even if the universe shall end

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.864
Even if the universe shall end
Teacher, are you mad?

00:03:16.864 --> 00:03:17.524
Even if the universe shall end

00:03:17.524 --> 00:03:17.594
Even if the universe shall end
It's not that I'm mad.

00:03:17.594 --> 00:03:17.624
It's not that I'm mad.

00:03:17.624 --> 00:03:19.864
And the lights of the stars may vanish
It's not that I'm mad.

00:03:19.864 --> 00:03:25.424
And the lights of the stars may vanish

00:03:25.604 --> 00:03:33.474
The light in your eyes

00:03:33.614 --> 00:03:41.074
Will continue to speak
of an endless journey

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:45.284
In The World

00:03:46.524 --> 00:03:49.044
Why did you call me here?

00:03:50.324 --> 00:03:51.354
Sorry.

00:03:51.724 --> 00:03:54.724
It doesn't feel right
to hear you apologize.

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:56.664
I see.

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:58.524
I guess you're right.

00:04:02.804 --> 00:04:07.004
In thirty minutes my account
will be suspended.

00:04:07.144 --> 00:04:09.404
You were notified?

00:04:11.744 --> 00:04:13.714
I am the face of TaN.

00:04:15.614 --> 00:04:17.174
I won't run away.

00:04:19.384 --> 00:04:20.374
That's honorable.

00:04:21.954 --> 00:04:24.114
It's not that it's honorable.

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:26.894
It's...

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:31.824
...my merchant's pride.

00:04:32.464 --> 00:04:34.764
I assume my own liabilities.

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:37.674
That's all there is to it.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:38.834
Right.

00:04:39.744 --> 00:04:42.434
Well, you gave me
a good lesson.

00:04:43.374 --> 00:04:46.404
By the way, would you do me a favor?

00:04:46.844 --> 00:04:49.284
Depends on what it is.

00:04:50.554 --> 00:04:55.714
The distorted graphics
found in the Lost Grounds.

00:04:55.794 --> 00:04:57.224
You've seen them before, right?

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:59.214
The triangles?

00:04:59.464 --> 00:05:00.424
Yeah.

00:05:00.564 --> 00:05:03.124
I've never seen a cheat
like that before.

00:05:03.604 --> 00:05:04.064
And?

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:06.824
We as TaN...

00:05:06.904 --> 00:05:12.564
...have been the ones promoting
all the hot trends since the new revision.

00:05:16.314 --> 00:05:17.374
"Signs".

00:05:18.014 --> 00:05:20.144
That's the name I'm giving them.

00:05:20.284 --> 00:05:21.254
Signs?

00:05:21.784 --> 00:05:24.654
If someone asks you,
tell them that.

00:05:25.184 --> 00:05:26.654
You think someone will ask?

00:05:26.924 --> 00:05:29.394
They're like omens.

00:05:29.824 --> 00:05:32.224
I named them with that in mind.

00:05:33.864 --> 00:05:37.664
The day will come when everyone
will be talking about Signs.

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:42.794
It's about time.

00:05:43.974 --> 00:05:44.874
Yeah?

00:05:47.274 --> 00:05:48.204
Later.

00:05:50.914 --> 00:05:53.504
If his account is being suspended...

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:57.444
...there won't be a "later".

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:01.314
Did he find the Key of the Twilight?

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:02.824
Or not?

00:06:03.254 --> 00:06:05.054
Didn't you at least ask him?

00:06:05.494 --> 00:06:07.824
I can't get in touch with him.

00:06:07.894 --> 00:06:10.524
I'm tired of hearing that.

00:06:10.934 --> 00:06:13.364
There's no use getting
worked up about it.

00:06:13.504 --> 00:06:15.494
No use, huh?

00:06:16.374 --> 00:06:18.564
Maybe he's hoarding it for himself!

00:06:22.614 --> 00:06:23.774
Sakisaka...

00:06:27.214 --> 00:06:30.614
Do you really think that?

00:06:32.084 --> 00:06:33.614
Just a little while longer.

00:06:33.924 --> 00:06:35.554
How much longer?

00:06:36.194 --> 00:06:39.254
There's a time limit
for everything, isn't there?

00:06:50.644 --> 00:06:51.904
Hey, you.

00:06:59.544 --> 00:07:00.744
Come over here.

00:07:10.294 --> 00:07:12.314
You shouldn't be so cheerful.

00:07:12.594 --> 00:07:13.684
Why not?

00:07:14.134 --> 00:07:16.464
What do you mean "why not"?

00:07:16.794 --> 00:07:19.524
Ovan hasn't come back yet, right?

00:07:19.964 --> 00:07:21.264
Aren't you worried?

00:07:21.704 --> 00:07:24.004
But he's never around.

00:07:24.144 --> 00:07:25.804
Besides, Shino's with us!

00:07:27.744 --> 00:07:30.804
Stop making excuses like
you're in junior high.

00:07:31.014 --> 00:07:32.414
You're wrong!

00:07:32.484 --> 00:07:35.074
I'm in senior high!
Though I may not seem like it.

00:07:37.584 --> 00:07:38.614
Haseo!

00:07:43.424 --> 00:07:44.224
What?

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.724
I was scolding her
for being so cheerful.

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:49.354
Can you take her with you?

00:07:49.434 --> 00:07:51.834
I didn't do anything
that deserves a scolding.

00:07:54.134 --> 00:07:55.104
So...

00:07:56.274 --> 00:07:58.744
...does it look like
Ovan might come back?

00:07:59.404 --> 00:08:00.634
I don't know.

00:08:01.074 --> 00:08:03.564
You're better off asking Shino.

00:08:04.884 --> 00:08:06.404
It's difficult to ask her.

00:08:07.114 --> 00:08:09.014
That's why I asked you.

00:08:10.054 --> 00:08:11.114
Right!

00:08:11.884 --> 00:08:13.824
We're heading back to ask Shino!

00:08:13.894 --> 00:08:15.114
H-Hey!

00:08:15.894 --> 00:08:17.184
Let go!

00:08:19.864 --> 00:08:23.884
The triangle graphics
in the Lost Grounds...

00:08:23.964 --> 00:08:25.434
...are called "Signs".

00:08:26.204 --> 00:08:27.934
That's what they're called?

00:08:28.504 --> 00:08:30.334
Yeah, they were just named.

00:08:30.844 --> 00:08:33.534
If someone asks,
you tell them that.

00:08:34.074 --> 00:08:35.164
Okay, but...

00:08:35.814 --> 00:08:38.074
Haseo, come on. Let's go.

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:39.744
Sign?

00:08:40.514 --> 00:08:41.544
A symbol?

00:08:50.864 --> 00:08:54.724
Where did you go?

00:09:02.874 --> 00:09:03.894
I...

00:09:19.884 --> 00:09:22.014
I'm gonna move on
from this game.

00:09:22.594 --> 00:09:23.554
I see.

00:09:24.524 --> 00:09:28.224
Besides, Ovan hasn't shown up.
It's high time.

00:09:30.434 --> 00:09:33.494
You've done a lot for me, old man.

00:09:34.074 --> 00:09:35.864
It was nothing.

00:09:35.974 --> 00:09:38.904
I'm just an old man passing time.

00:09:39.444 --> 00:09:41.344
Won't you be lonely?

00:09:42.874 --> 00:09:44.974
This is a playground.

00:09:45.744 --> 00:09:49.374
Everyone will be gone at some point.

00:09:50.624 --> 00:09:53.614
Like when you play at the
park in the evening...

00:09:53.684 --> 00:09:57.814
...and one by one,
your friends go home.

00:09:58.964 --> 00:10:01.394
Go home, huh?

00:10:02.294 --> 00:10:03.694
Are you going to be okay?

00:10:03.764 --> 00:10:04.894
What do you mean?

00:10:05.004 --> 00:10:06.664
The real you?

00:10:06.734 --> 00:10:09.264
That's why I'm leaving.

00:10:09.374 --> 00:10:12.734
I can't keep running away
from reality in here.

00:10:13.144 --> 00:10:15.334
Running away. I see.

00:10:16.244 --> 00:10:18.874
I plan to redeem myself.

00:10:22.384 --> 00:10:24.874
You can start over,
not only in the Net...

00:10:24.954 --> 00:10:27.044
...but in the real world as well.

00:10:29.154 --> 00:10:30.854
That would be nice.

00:10:37.734 --> 00:10:38.354
Huh?

00:10:44.874 --> 00:10:45.774
Teacher?

00:10:50.744 --> 00:10:52.404
What's up with him?

00:11:02.924 --> 00:11:04.224
Shino!

00:11:05.024 --> 00:11:07.964
We just saw Sakisaka leave.

00:11:08.494 --> 00:11:10.364
Yeah, I know.

00:11:10.934 --> 00:11:12.494
Did something happen?

00:11:13.504 --> 00:11:16.524
You guys don't need
to worry about it...

00:11:16.774 --> 00:11:18.504
...so don't look so sad.

00:11:51.044 --> 00:11:53.534
So you're here, as usual.

00:11:53.604 --> 00:11:56.664
Saves you from having to
look for me, doesn't it?

00:11:57.144 --> 00:12:00.774
Is it okay to be out right after
your guild was disbanded?

00:12:00.914 --> 00:12:02.714
I'm not concerned.

00:12:02.884 --> 00:12:03.944
I see.

00:12:04.354 --> 00:12:06.914
There are so many rumors around...

00:12:06.984 --> 00:12:10.224
...I thought you'd be
a little concerned.

00:12:10.424 --> 00:12:13.054
Today's the last day
for this character.

00:12:13.724 --> 00:12:15.454
I see.

00:12:15.764 --> 00:12:19.494
So I guess the rumors
don't faze you.

00:12:20.134 --> 00:12:22.504
What brings you here today?

00:12:23.074 --> 00:12:25.904
I have something to
tell you, old man.

00:12:26.204 --> 00:12:28.404
Let's go some place else.

00:12:29.314 --> 00:12:30.904
Here we go...

00:12:34.254 --> 00:12:36.874
Forget about Ovan.

00:12:38.254 --> 00:12:40.744
He can't come back anymore.

00:12:52.964 --> 00:12:53.864
Ovan...

00:13:02.344 --> 00:13:05.504
Seems like Teacher's still in the game.

00:13:05.684 --> 00:13:07.704
But he hasn't replied yet.

00:13:08.054 --> 00:13:10.914
How are you going to find him?

00:13:11.054 --> 00:13:12.484
What should we do?

00:13:12.724 --> 00:13:15.984
I'd call him if I knew his phone number.

00:13:16.054 --> 00:13:17.784
But he never gave it to me.

00:13:17.964 --> 00:13:19.514
Do you know it, Haseo?

00:13:19.764 --> 00:13:23.354
If you don't know it,
why would I?

00:13:23.534 --> 00:13:24.554
I guess you're right.

00:13:25.464 --> 00:13:27.524
Instead of wandering around...

00:13:27.604 --> 00:13:29.934
...it's probably
better to wait at home.

00:13:34.074 --> 00:13:34.874
What?

00:13:35.674 --> 00:13:38.234
You want to be with Shino that much?

00:13:38.314 --> 00:13:39.044
Huh?

00:13:39.414 --> 00:13:42.544
I've seen that look in your eyes before.

00:13:42.614 --> 00:13:44.584
Seemed kind of serious to me.

00:13:45.124 --> 00:13:48.024
What are you talking about?
This is a CG.

00:13:48.354 --> 00:13:49.184
No.

00:13:49.254 --> 00:13:51.924
I can tell you were gazing at her
through your display.

00:13:53.394 --> 00:13:56.724
Well, you can't really replace Ovan anyway.

00:13:57.194 --> 00:13:58.664
What do you mean by that?

00:13:58.804 --> 00:14:01.634
I mean you can't support Shino.

00:14:01.804 --> 00:14:04.794
And, you can support her?

00:14:04.874 --> 00:14:05.844
Probably...

00:14:08.174 --> 00:14:09.434
Probably not.

00:14:23.524 --> 00:14:27.364
It's unusual to see you here, Phyllo.

00:14:27.994 --> 00:14:28.694
Huh?

00:14:32.104 --> 00:14:34.864
You haven't seen him since he disappeared?

00:14:34.934 --> 00:14:35.734
No.

00:14:35.804 --> 00:14:36.774
Any contact?

00:14:39.174 --> 00:14:40.164
I see.

00:14:40.844 --> 00:14:42.314
So it's true.

00:14:43.014 --> 00:14:46.244
What do you mean, "it's true"?

00:14:50.954 --> 00:14:52.714
Phyllo...

00:14:53.224 --> 00:14:55.744
...what do you know?

00:14:56.224 --> 00:14:58.554
He wasn't in town.

00:14:58.764 --> 00:15:01.554
Let's check out the Lost Grounds.

00:15:01.734 --> 00:15:04.994
Or you could send him an email
telling him to come back.

00:15:05.064 --> 00:15:07.004
We might miss him.

00:15:07.264 --> 00:15:09.494
I told you he's not replying.

00:15:09.674 --> 00:15:11.534
That's not the problem.

00:15:27.554 --> 00:15:30.454
Oh! You're early!

00:15:31.664 --> 00:15:34.094
So that's one of them.

00:15:34.164 --> 00:15:36.964
The rumors say all
the Lost Grounds have them.

00:15:37.164 --> 00:15:38.994
They're called "Signs".

00:15:40.534 --> 00:15:43.764
I wonder if they're going to be used
in a new event or something?

00:15:45.444 --> 00:15:47.274
So, why did you want to see me?

00:15:47.344 --> 00:15:48.404
Oh, that's right!

00:15:48.774 --> 00:15:50.334
It's about Gord.

00:15:53.244 --> 00:15:57.114
He had a feeling from the beginning...

00:15:57.784 --> 00:15:59.914
...that it could be a trap.

00:16:00.654 --> 00:16:03.484
So even if he can't move right now...

00:16:03.554 --> 00:16:06.354
...I think he'll come back one day.

00:16:08.094 --> 00:16:09.064
But...

00:16:11.064 --> 00:16:12.694
...with the way things are...

00:16:12.764 --> 00:16:16.794
...I can't hold the Brigade together by myself.

00:16:19.274 --> 00:16:25.184
So Naobi was the one who told you
Ovan isn't returning?

00:16:25.444 --> 00:16:27.914
Why do you ask?

00:16:29.184 --> 00:16:33.674
You know the Ovan that I don't know.

00:16:34.794 --> 00:16:38.484
I thought you must know Naobi as well.

00:16:39.764 --> 00:16:41.824
It's just a woman's intuition.

00:16:42.934 --> 00:16:46.564
It's not like I think you and Naobi
are working together.

00:16:46.634 --> 00:16:47.654
Don't worry.

00:16:49.534 --> 00:16:50.834
Ovan...

00:16:52.104 --> 00:16:56.164
...wasn't able to find
the Key of the Twilight, right?

00:16:56.474 --> 00:16:59.574
Well, that's the way it is.

00:17:04.114 --> 00:17:05.174
Shino...

00:17:06.224 --> 00:17:07.214
It's okay.

00:17:07.894 --> 00:17:08.854
I think.

00:17:09.494 --> 00:17:13.154
Most importantly,
I need to tell everyone...

00:17:13.224 --> 00:17:14.024
...right?

00:17:27.344 --> 00:17:32.544
Ovan, is it really true
that you can't come back?

00:17:39.884 --> 00:17:44.124
Are you guys waiting
here for Sakisaka?

00:17:44.424 --> 00:17:47.324
No, we were about
to go looking for him.

00:17:47.494 --> 00:17:49.194
That's unnecessary.

00:17:49.664 --> 00:17:51.634
I'd like you to go home right away.

00:17:52.064 --> 00:17:53.624
Did something happen?

00:18:01.944 --> 00:18:04.134
I have news for everyone.

00:18:04.344 --> 00:18:05.404
Shino?

00:18:05.584 --> 00:18:08.104
Let's just go home first.

00:18:39.514 --> 00:18:42.604
After examining various reports...

00:18:43.614 --> 00:18:47.574
...I've come to realize that the
Key of the Twilight does not exist.

00:18:48.654 --> 00:18:50.784
It's not in this game?

00:18:50.994 --> 00:18:53.964
"Does not exist" means exactly that.

00:18:57.264 --> 00:18:58.094
What about Ovan?

00:19:00.804 --> 00:19:02.634
He ran into some trouble.

00:19:02.704 --> 00:19:05.224
I don't think he'll be
coming back for a while.

00:19:08.614 --> 00:19:10.274
Trouble or not...

00:19:10.344 --> 00:19:12.714
...if the Key of the Twilight
doesn't exist...

00:19:12.784 --> 00:19:14.544
...he can't come back.

00:19:14.954 --> 00:19:17.044
He won't be able to face us.

00:19:18.224 --> 00:19:20.554
So, what are we going to do now?

00:19:21.024 --> 00:19:24.924
So Ovan isn't coming back anymore?

00:19:26.094 --> 00:19:29.494
Does that mean we're going
to be disbanded like TaN?

00:19:29.694 --> 00:19:30.254
No.

00:19:30.664 --> 00:19:32.864
He'll come back after a while.

00:19:33.364 --> 00:19:34.354
It'll be alright.

00:19:35.104 --> 00:19:36.794
Then, let's wait!

00:19:37.034 --> 00:19:40.164
Besides, we're used to
not having Ovan around!

00:19:40.304 --> 00:19:40.864
Right?

00:19:41.174 --> 00:19:42.334
Are you an idiot?

00:19:42.714 --> 00:19:44.774
It's not the same as usual.

00:19:44.914 --> 00:19:47.504
There's no Key of the Twilight.

00:19:47.644 --> 00:19:49.484
There's no way he's coming back.

00:19:50.054 --> 00:19:51.174
Don't say that.

00:19:51.484 --> 00:19:53.254
He'll come back, for sure.

00:19:53.924 --> 00:19:55.184
What's your proof?

00:19:55.354 --> 00:19:57.384
There's no use arguing about it.

00:19:59.564 --> 00:20:03.294
Besides, it's not going
to bring Ovan back.

00:20:08.634 --> 00:20:09.434
Sorry.

00:20:09.804 --> 00:20:11.434
I'm going to go cool off.

00:20:12.104 --> 00:20:13.434
Sakisaka...

00:20:17.044 --> 00:20:18.744
I'll go check on Teacher!

00:20:24.084 --> 00:20:25.054
I'm sorry.

00:20:25.984 --> 00:20:28.614
There's no reason for you to apologize.

00:20:29.124 --> 00:20:29.924
But...

00:20:32.624 --> 00:20:33.524
Thank you.

00:20:34.994 --> 00:20:37.624
You don't need to thank me.

00:20:59.924 --> 00:21:02.824
I'm going to log out for today.

00:21:03.754 --> 00:21:05.524
Teacher, wait for me!

00:21:07.824 --> 00:21:09.024
Teacher...

00:21:12.964 --> 00:21:14.194
I said wait!

00:21:14.264 --> 00:21:15.824
Just leave me alone.

00:21:15.974 --> 00:21:16.694
I can't.

00:21:17.944 --> 00:21:20.404
I just want some time
to think on my own.

00:21:20.604 --> 00:21:22.574
What is there to think about?

00:21:23.344 --> 00:21:24.574
Lots of things.

00:21:25.444 --> 00:21:29.974
Are you going to leave
like Bset and Gord?

00:21:31.954 --> 00:21:32.974
Of course not.

00:21:33.924 --> 00:21:34.884
Right!

00:21:35.394 --> 00:21:37.724
Then let's go back! Come on!

00:21:37.824 --> 00:21:38.724
Let's go!

00:21:38.864 --> 00:21:39.754
Shut up!

00:21:43.364 --> 00:21:45.994
Why are you always so cheerful?

00:21:49.334 --> 00:21:51.364
It's not because I want to be!

00:22:29.514 --> 00:22:33.104
Ikiru wa dokuhai kiyu no kurushimi wo
Life is a poisoned cup of needless suffering

00:22:33.184 --> 00:22:36.614
Nomihosu sube wo dare ga sazukeyo
That no one can show me how to drain

00:22:36.884 --> 00:22:40.284
Taiyo ni sumu toiu kenja no washi
A wise eagle is said to live in the sun

00:22:40.354 --> 00:22:44.724
Habataki dake ga kodama suru
The flapping of its wings
is all that echoes

00:22:48.234 --> 00:22:51.754
Kono futatsu no me ni yadotta
In each of these eyes

00:22:51.834 --> 00:22:55.534
Yami to Hikari sono docchi de
Dwell darkness and light

00:22:55.604 --> 00:23:02.844
Boku wa ashita wo mitsumeru beki nano darou
Through which shall I look to tomorrow?

00:23:02.914 --> 00:23:06.574
Kawaki kitta gareki no machi
A dried out and ruined city

00:23:06.644 --> 00:23:10.344
Ten to sen wo tsunagi awase
Draws the lines between the dots

00:23:10.414 --> 00:23:17.344
Imi nado nai koto bakari afurete iku
Causing meaningless events to overflow

00:23:17.524 --> 00:23:21.254
Honou no gotoki kodoku
Soothing the loneliness

00:23:21.334 --> 00:23:24.354
Idaku karada shizumete wa
That flames up within the body

00:23:24.434 --> 00:23:31.894
Ankyo eto shitatatte iku shizuku
Droplets of water fall towards the culvert

00:23:32.144 --> 00:23:35.334
Kakageru dokuhai kono sei wa michitemo
Even if the poisoned cup is upheld
and filled with this life

00:23:35.414 --> 00:23:39.434
Kogareru shino yume wa nagare tsuku
My dream that yearns for death
drifts into it

00:23:39.544 --> 00:23:43.144
Toride ni kuikomu tsume kokou no washi
The eagle remains aloof;
its talons dig into the fort

00:23:43.214 --> 00:23:46.774
Habataki dake ga maiagaru
Only the flapping of its wings resounds

00:23:46.854 --> 00:23:50.584
Ano soukyu ni takkei ni shite kure tamae
Let me be crucified in the blue sky

00:23:50.654 --> 00:23:54.354
Ten to chi ga musubu basho ni
bokuwa tatsu
I'll stand where heaven and earth meet

00:23:55.364 --> 00:23:56.454
Next Episode
